  "version": "1.0",
  "release_date": "2025-06-06T00:00:00Z",
  "updated": "2025-06-06T00:00:00Z",
  "description": "TerraFM is a scalable self-supervised foundation model for unified multisensor Earth observation, leveraging globally distributed Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 imagery with large spatial tiles and land-cover aware sampling. It unifies radar and optical inputs via modality-specific patch embeddings and adaptive cross-attention fusion, and introduces dual-centering for class-frequency-aware regularization. TerraFM achieves state-of-the-art results on GEO-Bench and Copernicus-Bench for classification and segmentation tasks.",
  "sci:doi": "10.48550/arXiv.2506.06281",
